tip: | Look at the gardener. | A wide hat and a long-handled spade say gardener before any detail does. Cover them with a thumb and it could be anyone.
tip: 1 | Silhouette first. | Hat brim wider than the shoulders, tool taller than the head. Props that stick out of the shape read best.
tip: 3 | Each garment a ramp. | Straw, shirt, overalls and skin each step along their own ramp, so clothes look like separate things and not one painted shape.
tip: 4 | Shade under the brim. | One dark row across the top of the face puts the hat on the head. Without it the hat floats.
